      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Evaluate $Γ(\\frac{3}{2}).$",
      "worked_solution": "To evaluate the gamma function at multiples of one-half, we use the following recursive formula:\n\n$$\nΓ(z+1)=zΓ(z),\\,Γ(\\frac{1}{2})=\\sqrt{\\pi }\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Γ(\\frac{3}{2}) & =\\frac{1}{2}Γ(\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{\\pi }}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
